  // Sign sizes and supplementary plates. speedBandsKph are the six 85th percentile speed bands
  // of TSM Chapter 4 Appendix A and Chapter 3 Appendix A (up to 20, 21-30, 31-40, 41-50, 51-60,
  // over 60 mph), with upper bounds converted to km/h by rounding down as for textSizes above.
  //
  // A plate carries the legend of an associated plate (TSRGD Schedule 2 Part 2 column 4,
  // Schedule 3 Part 3) and is designed as the Chapter 7 Figure 2-4 plate (panel and signBorder
  // above). Its x-height comes from the row of the plate size table that covers its legend
  // (pattern: a regular expression over the legend, lines joined by a space). A legend no row
  // covers is not drawn and raises PLATE_SIZE_UNSPECIFIED.
  //   Warning plates: TSM Chapter 4 Appendix B, by triangle height. A "50/62.5" cell gives 50 mm
  //   where the 85th percentile speed is 20 mph or less (note 1), else 62.5. The larger value of a
  //   "125/150" cell is for dual carriageways (note 2); a schedule row does not say which road it
  //   is on, so 125 is used.
  //   Regulatory plates: TSM Chapter 3 Appendix A row 570 ("For" and a distance), by speed band.
  // Gap between sign and plate: neither TSRGD nor TSM Chapters 3 and 4 state one in general.
  // Chapter 3 paras 1.28 and 14.60 butt an "End" or distance plate up to a clearway sign, which is
  // the closest rule; gapMm is null for both families, so the plate is butted to the sign and
  // PLATE_GAP_UNSPECIFIED is raised.
